    "S02": "same-prefix variants keep execution and unknown spans open",
    "S03": "update/modify objects split language behavior from targets",
    "S04": "unmet conditions stay pending without automation or steering",
    "S05": "first-step and persisted-input visibility with the same closure",
    "S06": "trusted host selections and separate approval records",
    "S07": "clarification supersedes atomically; unrelated tasks never collide",
    "S08": "turn structure gates delivery; delegation never closes the parent",
    "S09": "requested visual and readback proof stays unavailable when no producer exists",
    "S10": "policy tiers are orthogonal to activation and never block ordinary work",
    "S11": "the explicit release ticket refuses every wrong or consumed adoption",
    "S12": "legacy and v5 sessions report their own rule set and keep old identities"
